   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have the following model I wish to express syntactically:<div><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-b2XsAR1Vc3w/U5GwJLMlOMI/AAAAAAAAAN0/Wp7SbqAiZRE/s1600/pathModel.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-b2XsAR1Vc3w/U5GwJLMlOMI/AAAAAAAAAN0/Wp7SbqAiZRE/s1600/pathModel.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22Jmnhqm8wnJkwz1AWBTV3\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-b2XsAR1Vc3w/U5GwJLMlOMI/AAAAAAAAAN0/Wp7SbqAiZRE/s320/pathModel.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"170\"></a></p><div>If it were only a matter of mediation, I know that I&#39;d just use:</div></div><div>\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\t<div title=\"Page 28\">\r\n\t\t\t<div>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; # direct effect <br></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#080\">+  Y~c*X </span></span><span style=\"color:#080\"><br>+ # mediator <br>+ M~a*X <br>+ Y~b*M <br>+ # indirect effect (a*b)<br></span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#080\">+  ab := a*b </span></span><span style=\"color:#080\"><br>+ # total effect<br>+ total := c + (a*b) +&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\"><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\"><br></span></div>However, I&#39;m unsure how to specify the moderators in the analysis. Would it just be a case of adding:</span><br>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M<br>Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span></div></code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\"><br></span></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">to the model specification? I know that you can specify a separate regression coefficient per group if your moderator is categorical (see </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ\" style=\"line-height:18px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483943000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1HnREm4fq90vt4D4NQf76u\">here</a><span style=\"line-height:18px\">), but I don&#39;t think that applies here as all variables are continuous.</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">Any guidance is much appreciated!</span></font></div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
