   "subject": "Re: Moderated mediation (path analysis) when all variables are continuous",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div title=\"Page 28\"><div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\">However, I&#39;m unsure how to specify the moderators in the analysis. Would it just be a case of adding:</span><br>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M<br>Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span></div></code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\"><br></span></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">to the model specification? I know that you can specify a separate regression coefficient per group if your moderator is categorical (see </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ\" style=\"line-height:18px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw197CeDWKH9L12QEoAq_Tgv\">here</a><span style=\"line-height:18px\">), but I don&#39;t think that applies here as all variables are continuous.</span></font></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;m not sure whether this allows you to estimated moderated mediation in lavaan, but to use interaction terms in the lavaan syntax, you&#39;ll need to manually calculate the product term in your data.frame.  And as such, you&#39;ll need to give them appropriate names (i.e., without the colon).  For example, you could create product term for Z times Y called ZY, then include &#39; Y ~ ZY &#39; in your syntax.</div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "XZGiqbiFOLYJ",
   "from": "Alex Schoemann",
   "author": "5d4f9e7f97c21008",
   "date": "2014-06-06T16:46:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: Moderated mediation (path analysis) when all variables are continuous",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">To add to Terrys comment. You can fit the model in lavaan but you&#39;ll need to specify all conditional indirect effects by hand. I&#39;d recommend taking a look at the following paper, which  describes the issue and has accompanying Mplus code for some similar models (here: <a href=\"http://www.afhayes.com/public/mplus1to5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.afhayes.com/public/mplus1to5.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1w99ajd2bVG4IcOoW-eL0o\">http://www.afhayes.com/public/mplus1to5.pdf</a>):<div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(98,98,98);font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:bold\">Preacher, K. J., Rucker, D. D., &amp; Hayes, A. F. (2007).  Assessing moderated mediation hypotheses: Theory, methods, and prescriptions.  </span><em style=\"color:rgb(98,98,98);font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:bold\">Multivariate Behavioral Research, 42</em><span style=\"color:rgb(98,98,98);font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;font-weight:bold\">, 185-227.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(98,98,98);font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px\"> </span><a title=\"\" href=\"http://www.quantpsy.org/pubs/preacher_rucker_hayes_2007.pdf\" style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(76,170,201)!important\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.quantpsy.org/pubs/preacher_rucker_hayes_2007.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mljFrEMhK-Nvm2k-AZ1r0\">[</a><a title=\"\" href=\"http://www.quantpsy.org/pubs/preacher_rucker_hayes_2007.pdf\" style=\"font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:rgb(76,170,201)!important\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.quantpsy.org/pubs/preacher_rucker_hayes_2007.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mljFrEMhK-Nvm2k-AZ1r0\">PDF</a><span style=\"color:rgb(98,98,98);font-family:Tahoma,Geneva,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px\">]</span><br><br>Alex</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Friday, June 6, 2014 12:23:00 PM UTC-4, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div title=\"Page 28\"><div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\">However, I&#39;m unsure how to specify the moderators in the analysis. Would it just be a case of adding:</span><br>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M<br>Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span></div></code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:18px\"><br></span></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">to the model specification? I know that you can specify a separate regression coefficient per group if your moderator is categorical (see </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ\" style=\"line-height:18px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792431483945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2I2MRaCVSWPE0koa6DMS9e\">here</a><span style=\"line-height:18px\">), but I don&#39;t think that applies here as all variables are continuous.</span></font></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m not sure whether this allows you to estimated moderated mediation in lavaan, but to use interaction terms in the lavaan syntax, you&#39;ll need to manually calculate the product term in your data.frame.  And as such, you&#39;ll need to give them appropriate names (i.e., without the colon).  For example, you could create product term for Z times Y called ZY, then include &#39; Y ~ ZY &#39; in your syntax.</div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
